# Fire Lord Sozin: "you may pay {X}. When you do, put any number of target creature cards ... onto the battlefield under your
# control." Declining is not doing it (CR 603.12): the reflexive ability never triggers, so no target is asked for and Bot2's
# graveyard keeps its creature cards. The firebending mana is not spent, and is lost as combat ends.
#
# Bot2's creatures, cast on T2, die to chapter I on T3; chapter III returns the Saga as Fire Lord Sozin on T7, and on T9 it attacks
# and deals 5 combat damage to Bot2. Bot1 declines the payment; the bare refusal proves no target question follows before its next
# priority (the positive control is fire-lord-sozin-pays-x-and-returns-creature-cards-with-total-mana-value-x-or-less, where the
# same position pays and is asked).

